Original commit body from 0e2d51f6a1d57284eb6635d9a182192e2135518e:

WI-logad, WI-hofav, WI-sohov. Three items, one spec section, each claim
wrong in a different way.

WI-logad — the tier table omitted the base most entrypoints carry. It
listed 0.99/0.95/0.85/0.80/0.70/0.50 and named neither 0.75 nor 0.90.
library_export emits 0.75 and is the single most common entrypoint kind on
the self-corpus (45 of 118, 38%), so the table was missing the plurality
case; 0.90 (FORM, SERIALIZER) was missing too. Both rows added, each
annotated with the evidence_type carrying it. The 0.70 and 0.50 rows are
KEPT despite being unexercised here — they are live producer constants
(naming_heuristic :1062, connectivity_heuristic :1368), and deleting a tier
because one corpus does not exercise it is the INV-lifik mistake.

WI-hofav — the claimed 1:1 mapping between evidence_type and confidence
does not hold. Measured, it fails for three of four emitted pathways:
framework_pattern {0.95, 0.90}, structural {0.85, 0.80},
language_convention {0.80, 0.75}; only manifest_declared {0.99} is
single-valued. The base is chosen per DETECTOR and several detectors share
a pathway at different bases, so evidence_type is documented as a coarser
grouping and consumers are told to read confidence directly.

WI-sohov — the discrete-vs-continuous contradiction was two descriptions
of what are now two different fields. The section still said penalties
apply to confidence and that ADR-0039's move to rank_score was "slated";
it shipped. confidence is pure detection reliability holding only the base;
rank_score takes the adjustments (test x0.1, vendor tier>=3 x0.3, utility
x0.5, plus an additive min(0.25, log(1+out_edges)/10) boost from which
deliberately demoted entries are excluded so an additive boost cannot undo
a multiplicative demotion).

Also: sorting was documented on the wrong key. The spec said "ranked by
confidence"; entrypoints.py:1600 sorts by rank_score, and the emitted array
is verifiably ordered by rank_score and NOT by confidence. The spec and the
two producer docstrings that repeated the stale claim are corrected, so the
contradiction cannot be restored from the code side.

Docs only; no emitted value changed. 2003 passed across the 42-file set.

